\cf1\fs32 New Features\par
\pard{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf5\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\nowidctlpar\fi-360\li720\sl240\slmult0\tx720\cf0\b0\fs24 New capability: CORACQ_CAP_SHAFT_ENCODER_REVERSE_COUNT_MAX. Previous driver was limited to a maximum count of 255. This has been increased to 65535.\cf2\par
\cf0{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}New parameter: CORACQ_PRM_SHAFT_ENCODER_REVERSE_COUNT: permits reading and resetting the shaft encoder reverse count.\cf2\par
\cf0{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Increased the maximum FFC gain for pixels > 8 bits from 2x to 8x.\cf2\par
\cf0{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Added support for CORACQ_PRM_EXT_TRIGGER_IGNORE_DELAY.\cf2\par
\cf0{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Increase horizontal flipping maximum line size from 16 kBytes to 64 kBytes.\cf2\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}New capability and parameter: CORACQ_CAP_META_DATA and CORACQ_PRM_META_DATA. Supported location is: CORACQ_VAL_META_DATA_PER_LINE_RIGHT\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Support for up to 4 mono planes. \par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Support for 2-channels, 2-taps, 14-bits monochrome.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Suppport for no roll-over when grabbing variable frame length images with external trigger set to rising/falling edge detection.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Support for 2T of 14B/16B.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Internal Line Trigger, Shaft Encoder Before and After Multiple/Drop can now be sent through board sync.\par
\pard{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf5\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\nowidctlpar\fi-360\li720\cf0 Horizontal flipping when output format is RGB888.\par
\pard{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf5\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\nowidctlpar\fi-360\li720\tx720 Windows 10 drivers are now signed with the Microsoft Windows Hardware Compatibility Publisher certificate.\cf2\par
\cf0{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Added support for flash parts from multiple vendors.\cf2\par
\cf0\f2{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Increase horizontal flipping maximum line size from 16 kBytes to 64 kBytes.\cf2\f0\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}New capability and parameter: CORACQ_CAP_META_DATA and CORACQ_PRM_META_DATA. Supported location is: CORACQ_VAL_META_DATA_PER_LINE_RIGHT\par
\pard{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlcont\pnf5\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\nowidctlpar\cf0\fs20\par
\cf1\b\fs32{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Fixes\cf0\fs20\par
\pard{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf5\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\nowidctlpar\fi-360\li720\sl240\slmult0\tx720\cf2\b0\fs24 On some boards, if serial port was opened with no camera connected, a flood of events could occur.\f1\tab\cf0\f0\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}BSOD would occur on systems where the PCIe bridge generates PnP events 'Remove/Add Device' following a reset of the board.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}DMA engine could stay in an invalid state necessitating a reset of the board when application is abrutly terminated (such as with Windows Task Manager) while grabbing.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Possible crash when coming back from Windows 8/10 Hybrid Shutdown if board shares it's interrupt with another device.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Application controlling 2 Xfers (multiple cameras), when disconnecting an Xfer, application would stop receiving Xfer events for the other active Xfer.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}On Abort command, if the number of on-board buffers ready to be transfered to host buffers are not transfered within 1 second, the error No EOT would occur and would prevent starting a grab.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Snap of free-running linescan camera could take up to 2 frame time to acquire.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Possible BSOD when resetting the board. Error returned by system makes reference to PCIe Completion Timeout.\par
\lang1033\f2{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Memory Controller calibration failure.\par
\pard\nowidctlpar\fi-720\li720\tx1440\lang4105\f0\par
