\pard{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlcont\pnf5\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\nowidctlpar\fi-360\li720\tx1440\cf2\b0\f1\fs24\'b7\tab\cf0\f0 Extra Xfer 'n' lines event generated when starting a grab.\cf2\par
\pard{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf5\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\nowidctlpar\fi-360\li720\tx1440\cf0 Shaft Encoder selection for the 2nd camera was not independent: it was following the selection of the 1st camera.\cf2\par
\cf0{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}External Line Trigger detection when used with dual camera was not independent: They would either be both rising or falling edge.\cf2\par
\pard{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf5\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\nowidctlpar\fi-360\li720\sl240\slmult0\tx720 Support for PCIe Maximum Read Request > 1K. 2K and 4K would crash PC.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Possible training issue at cold boot in some PCs.\par
\cf0{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}In Area Scan mode, if 2 image buffers did not fit in on-board memory, no errors were reported and part of the image that exceeded the on-board memory would be invalid in host memory. Driver will now treat this condition similar to linescan mode and will use 2 smaller on-board buffers. \cf2\par
\cf0\f2{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Integrated auto-calibration of the General Input Level Switch point for better accuracy.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}CorDeviceManager v3.73 fixes crash that would occur on W10 64-bit when clicking the "Browse..." button used to get a firmware CBF file.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Strobe output of Camera #2 (dual camera) was programming the physical Strobe #1 instead of physical Strobe #2.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Fix feeding of free buffers in HW queue in dual camera when there is more than 1024 host buffers for either or both cameras.\par
